    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve the performance of the n-body simulation by utilizing OpenMP for parallel processing.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Add OpenMP directives to parallelize the loop that updates the positions and velocities of particles.\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"/*\\n * n-body simulation with OpenMP parallelization\\n */\\n\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nstruct Particle {\\n    float x, y, z;\\n    float vx, vy, vz;\\n};\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n;\\n    std::cin >> n;\\n    std::vector<Particle> particles(n);\\n\\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {\\n        std::cin >> particles[i].x >> particles[i].y >> particles[i].z;\\n        std::cin >> particles[i].vx >> particles[i].vy >> particles[i].vz;\\n    }\\n\\n    assert(n<8000);\\n\\n    const float G = 6.67430e-11; // Gravitational constant\\n    const float dt = 0.001; // Time step\\n\\n    for(int t=0;t<1000;t++) {\\n        #pragma omp parallel for\\n        for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {\\n            for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++) {\\n                float dx = particles[j].x - particles[i].x;\\n                float dy = particles[j].y - particles[i].y;\\n                float dz = particles[j].z - particles[i].z;\\n                float r = std::sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz);\\n\\n                float force = G * particles[i].m * particles[j].m / (r*r);\\n\\n                float fx = force * dx / r;\\n                float fy = force * dy / r;\\n                float fz = force * dz / r;\\n\\n                particles[i].vx += fx * dt;\\n                particles[i].vy += fy * dt;\\n                particles[i].vz += fz * dt;\\n\\n                particles[j].vx -= fx * dt;\\n                particles[j].vy -= fy * dt;\\n                particles[j].vz -= fz * dt;\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        #pragma omp parallel for\\n        for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {\\n            particles[i].x += particles[i].vx * dt;\\n            particles[i].y += particles[i].vy * dt;\\n            particles[i].z += particles[i].vz * dt;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {\\n        std::cout << particles[i].x << \\\" \\\" << particles[i].y << \\\" \\\" << particles[i].z << std::endl;\\n    }\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"This transformation adds OpenMP directives to parallelize the loops that update the positions and velocities of particles, which can significantly improve the performance of the n-body simulation.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [],\n    \"urls\": []\n  }\n}"
